Objective
Provision a raw Linux remote host (or VM / Cloud instance) and transform it into a hardened, production-ready server. 
You will configure passwordless SSH key authentication, disable high-risk attack vectors (root logins & password prompts), 
change the default SSH port, configure an active firewall (UFW), and set up a non-root administrative user with scoped sudo privileges.
